 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a19-v02",
  "song": "tsa-a19",
  "verse": 2,
  "quick_english": "Therein, whatever rite was told for raising the dead — all of it is to be done to the body: by the full oblation, the burning of the corpse-body. But for the deluded, to plant conviction, let him perform, with the force of ritual-knowledge-yoga, a trust-bearing funeral rite; therein, on the corpse-body, having placed mantras in the withdrawing order, having drawn them in by the net-sequence, having done curbing-piercing-rubbing and the rest, let him do, by the breath-moving sequence, in heart, throat, forehead — and lo, the corpse-body trembles.",
