 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a19-v04",
  "song": "tsa-a19",
  "verse": 4,
  "quick_english": "Therein, having performed the rite ending in oblation, having made a food-offering in one hand, having meditated on his power of virile form, knowable-formed, that has attained identity with the knowable-power present in the beast — let him offer it to the Lord as enjoyer. Thus, when knowable-being ceases, he becomes the Lord himself. Whether by funeral-raising-śrāddha-initiations one has succeeded or not, still, for one desiring enjoyment, multitude of rites for multitude of fruit — thus, let him perform all.",
